A more promising variance reducer is to Gaussianize only the final pre-activation: use the sample mean and variance of the last-layer logits, then apply the exact scalar ReLU moment formula. That targets the scored layer directly and costs almost nothing. I’ll test blends of sampled final mean and Gaussianized final mean locally.
